{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude","imports":["lean:module:Init"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.naive_uniform_z_dead_across_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.naive_uniform_z_dead_across_A","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.lean#L115-L121","doc":"**Uniform `z` is dead across A.**  It is scope-(b) EXCLUDED where it is NEEDED\n(A=4: `det < 0`) and INSUFFICIENT where it is PHYSICAL (A=2: one interface factor\n`< 2×`, far below the `5.85×` deficit).  No single derived per-pair magnitude\n`z = 1/[2]_v` supplies the deuteron binding magnitude. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.deuteron_not_singlet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.deuteron_not_singlet","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.lean#L110-L111","doc":"`A = 2` is NOT a `[1^A]` singlet: `C(4,2) = 6 ≠ 1 = C(4,4)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.choose4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.choose4","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.lean#L101-L108","doc":"Binomial `C(4,k)` (finite, decidable). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.one_interface_factor_insufficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.one_interface_factor_insufficient","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.lean#L89-L92","doc":"**Single interface factor is insufficient.**  Even the over-generous doubling\nbound `2·B_cat` (the sup of `B_cat/(1 − z²)` since `1/(1−z²) < 2`) falls short of\n`B_AME`: `2·B_cat < B_AME`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.BAmeMilli","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.BAmeMilli","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.lean#L86-L87","doc":"AME2020 deuteron binding in `10⁻³ MeV` (diagnostic bound only, never inverted). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.BcatMilli","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.BcatMilli","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.lean#L84-L85","doc":"Master-Σ deuteron binding in `10⁻³ MeV` (committed `|S(D)| = 0.7438`, `m_e`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.z_sq_lt_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.z_sq_lt_half","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.lean#L81-L82","doc":"`z² < 1/2`: `2·zHi² < zDen²`.  (⟹ `1 − z² > 1/2` ⟹ interface factor `< 2`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.z_physical_A2_but_excluded_A4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.z_physical_A2_but_excluded_A4","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.lean#L63-L68","doc":"**The physicality SPLIT** (the derived cited invariant): the very same derived\n`z` gives a positive A=2 determinant and a negative A=4 first factor.  The A=4\nwrithe ceiling `1/√5` is below `z`; the A=2 ceiling `1` is above it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.detHe4_factor_neg_scaled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.detHe4_factor_neg_scaled","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.lean#L59-L61","doc":"The A=4 factor `1 − 5z²` is strictly negative (scaled form):\n`zDen² − 5·zLo² < 0`, so `det(I+zS) < 0` at A=4 — no attractive `−ln det` branch. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.z_excluded_at_A4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.z_excluded_at_A4","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.detK2_pos_scaled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.detK2_pos_scaled","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.lean#L49-L51","doc":"The A=2 interface determinant `1 − z²` is strictly positive (scaled form):\n`zDen² − zHi² > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.z_physical_at_A2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.z_physical_at_A2","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.zDen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.zDen","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.lean#L40-L41","doc":"Common denominator for the rational enclosure of `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.zHi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.zHi","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.lean#L38-L39","doc":"Numerator upper bound of `z` over `D = 10000`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.zLo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.zLo","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronNaiveZMagnitude.lean#L36-L37","doc":"Numerator lower bound of `z` over `D = 10000`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}